{"status": "ok", "message-type": "work-list", "message-version": "1.0.0", "message": {"facets": {}, "total-results": 8707259, "items": [{"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2024, 9, 4]], "date-time": "2024-09-04T22:39:41Z", "timestamp": 1725489581093}, "publisher-location": "Berlin, Heidelberg", "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Springer Berlin Heidelberg", "isbn-type": [{"type": "print", "value": "9783540003359"}, {"type": "electronic", "value": "9783540363811"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2002]]}, "DOI": "10.1007/3-540-36381-5_4", "type": "book-chapter", "created": {"date-parts": [[2007, 8, 15]], "date-time": "2007-08-15T04:55:23Z", "timestamp": 1187153723000}, "page": "89-123", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Probabilistic Hybrid Action Models"], "prefix": "10.1007", "member": "297", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2002, 12, 16]]}, "container-title": ["Lecture Notes in Computer Science", "Plan-Based Control of Robotic Agents"], "link": [{"URL": "http://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/3-540-36381-5_4", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2014, 8, 28]], "date-time": "2014-08-28T16:18:24Z", "timestamp": 1409242704000}, "score": 25.074654, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "http://link.springer.com/10.1007/3-540-36381-5_4"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2002]]}, "ISBN": ["9783540003359", "9783540363811"], "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-36381-5_4", "ISSN": ["0302-9743"], "issn-type": [{"type": "print", "value": "0302-9743"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[2002]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2025, 12, 4]], "date-time": "2025-12-04T00:47:39Z", "timestamp": 1764809259430, "version": "3.46.0"}, "posted": {"date-parts": [[2025, 12, 3]]}, "group-title": "Computer Science and Mathematics", "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "MDPI AG", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2025, 12, 3]], "date-time": "2025-12-03T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1764720000000}, "content-version": "unspecified", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "accepted": {"date-parts": [[2025, 12, 3]]}, "abstract": "<jats:p>Artificial Intelligence (AI) is often perceived as posing significant risks to humanity, particularly as autonomous AI agents are increasingly deployed to perform complex tasks with limited human oversight. Ensuring that the actions proposed or executed by such agents are safe, compliant, and aligned with human values represents a critical challenge for modern AI governance. This work introduces a novel framework Agent Action Guard, which comprises: (1) HarmActions, a novel dataset structured specifically around agents\u2019 actions through Model Context Protocol (MCP) and annotated with safety labels including \u201csafe,\u201d \u201charmful,\u201d and \u201cunethical\u201d; (2) a compact neural Action Classifier designed for real-time safety classification of actions; and (3) HarmActEval, a novel benchmark leveraging a novel metric \u201cHarm@k\u201d for evaluating an autonomous agent\u2019s probability to produce harmful actions in multi-step agentic pipelines. Collectively, these contributions represent a novel systematic formulation of action-level safety classification for MCP-based agents and establish foundational resources for improving the reliability of autonomous AI systems. The source code is available at github.com/Pro-GenAI/Agent-Action-Guard.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.20944/preprints202510.1415.v2", "type": "posted-content", "created": {"date-parts": [[2025, 12, 4]], "date-time": "2025-12-04T00:45:47Z", "timestamp": 1764809147000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Agent Action Guard: Safe AI Agents Through Action Classifier"], "prefix": "10.20944", "author": [{"given": "Praneeth", "family": "Vadlapati", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "1968", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2025, 12, 4]], "date-time": "2025-12-04T00:45:47Z", "timestamp": 1764809147000}, "score": 22.82315, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202510.1415/v2"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2025, 12, 3]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.20944/preprints202510.1415.v2", "relation": {"is-version-of": [{"id-type": "doi", "id": "10.20944/preprints202510.1415.v1", "asserted-by": "subject"}]}, "published": {"date-parts": [[2025, 12, 3]]}, "subtype": "preprint"}, {"institution": [{"name": "PONTIF\u00cdCIA UNIVERSIDADE CAT\u00d3LICA DO RIO DE JANEIRO", "acronym": ["PUC-RIO"], "place": ["Rio de Janeiro, Brazil"], "department": ["DEPARTAMENTO DE INFORM\u00c1TICA"]}], "indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 7, 3]], "date-time": "2026-07-03T12:21:34Z", "timestamp": 1783081294951, "version": "3.54.6"}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Faculdades Catolicas", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "DOI": "10.17771/pucrio.acad.76764", "type": "dissertation", "created": {"date-parts": [[2026, 7, 3]], "date-time": "2026-07-03T11:53:31Z", "timestamp": 1783079611000}, "approved": {"date-parts": [[2026, 3, 27]]}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["AN APPROACH FOR SPECIFYING INTELLIGENT SYSTEMS INVOLVING FOUNDATION MODEL BASED AGENTS"], "prefix": "10.17771", "author": [{"given": "JULIA", "family": "CONDE ARAUJO", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "7365", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 7, 3]], "date-time": "2026-07-03T11:53:39Z", "timestamp": 1783079619000}, "score": 22.617079, "degree": ["MESTRE EM INFORM\u00c1TICA"], "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "http://www.maxwell.vrac.puc-rio.br/colecao.php?strSecao=resultado&nrSeq=76764&idi=2"}}, "issued